## 2. 🔴 Two compliance defects (fix before the guías are filed)

**a) FE I lab hours do not close.** `tracks.yml` `fei:` sums `labHours` to **32.0 h** across 29 sessions. The official allocation is **30 h**. Phase 1's gate recorded this as passing; it does not. **2 h must come out** — a pedagogical decision, so I have not redistributed them silently. FE II is correct at 30.0 h.

**b) Two of three activity types are unallocated, in both courses.** `magistralHours` and `ejerciciosHours` appear **zero times**. The official split is **Lección Magistral 10 h / Prácticas de Laboratorio 30 h / Resolución de Ejercicios 14 h**. Only the middle one exists in data.

> This is what makes the `ACTIVIDADES FORMATIVAS` table unfillable truthfully — the original purpose of IGNITOR rule 2b, which covered lab hours only. Until fixed, any per-session hour claim to the department is unsupported.

---

## 3. Path to ready — ordered by what unblocks teaching

**Wave 0 — before any teaching (≈ half a day)**
1. Resolve the FE I 32 → 30 h discrepancy (your call which sessions).
2. Add `magistralHours` + `ejerciciosHours` to every session in both tracks; totals must close at 10 / 14.
3. Freeze and version the oral-defence rubric and AI-declaration template (also a research prerequisite, §4).

**Wave 1 — Units 11 + 12 (best evidenced; they define the assessment students meet)**
Forge per [`fe-unit-forge.mdc`](./fe-unit-forge.mdc): lesson + lab brief + exercise set. Evidence is ready — Garcia, Nelson & Ponciano, Vega (incremental PBL), González-Videgaray, Liu p.12 verbatim, DEC LATAM 65 %/56 %, Neumann (eduScrum) for the team-repo model.

**Wave 2 — Units 2 + 3 + 4** — the platform the frontier needs. All three **declare a gap**; ground technique in dated vendor docs only.

**Wave 3 — Units 8 + 9 + 10** — the frontier. Declare pilot. Neelakantam & Pant grounds *technique* for 8–9 only.

**Wave 4 — Units 1 + 7** — kickoff last (it must promise what the other eleven deliver); Unit 7 already has its ethics section, needs lab + exercises.

**Wave 5 — 12 decks.** After prose settles. A deck for a lesson still in flux is waste.

**Minimum viable to start the semester:** Wave 0 + Wave 1 + Unit 2. Weeks 3–4 of teaching can run one wave ahead of delivery if necessary — but not more, and the exercise sets cannot be the thing that slips, because they are the individual-evidence channel (§4).

