## 4. Research layer — status against the vaults

**Grounding is current.** All vaults are registered and classed in [`grounding/README.mdc`](./grounding/README.mdc): `fe-main` (18 coats), `fe-ibero` (8), and four cross-project SVCM vaults with explicit *"never use for"* rules. The **discover-in-vectors / cite-from-nodes** rule is recorded. 21 strict coat·node citations across the guías resolve, including the UNESCO coat.

**Recent movement:** three gaps closed (eduScrum → team repo; Vega → incremental PBL; Burgos → ethics-first, first Spain-inclusive source), one reclassified (energy → normative via UNESCO), two refused (O'Toole homonym; WebVR-as-pedagogy).

**Still open, deliberately:** six FE II units unevidenced (the pilot thesis); the empirical energy claim; Spanish legal instruments not ingested; Taylor's archive/repertoire cited nowhere pending a definitional node.

**🔴 What is NOT ready:** the human layer.

| Prerequisite | State |
| --- | --- |
| Consent set C1–C4 drafted and IP-administered | ✗ not started |
| RGPD basis + DPO sign-off (UDIT) | ✗ not started |
| Second-institution approval (UEM, for the synergy) | ✗ not started |
| Instruments frozen and versioned | ✗ not done (Wave 0.3) |

**Consequence, stated plainly:** teaching can begin without any of these. **Research data cannot be collected without them.** If September starts unconsented, 2026-27 yields a taught course and no usable dataset — the arc restarts in 2027-28.

